    "summary": "I built a one-cell storage box: a full hex base with a full-depth bin inside and a full cover on top as the lid. The lid is held shut by magnets: the parts list has 6 Ø5×1 mm neodymium disc magnets and 6 steel BBs for the cover. Magnets were already on when I fitted the cover, so turning them on reported \"no change\". I also put solid end caps on all six open side faces and ran the joint-locking step, which had nothing to bolt on a single cell. The build check found no rule issues and no mesh clashes. It has 12 printed parts, about 629 g of filament and about 857 minutes of printing. I added no props because the brief is about the box itself.",
